Two common constructions are mixtures (for arbitrary $S$ ) and geometric averages (for $S=\mathbb{R}^{d}$ ):

$$
\begin{aligned}
& p_{t}(d x | z)=\left(1-\kappa_{t}\right) \cdot p_{\text {simple }}(d x)+\kappa_{t} \cdot \delta_{z}(d x) \Leftrightarrow x_{t} \sim\left\{\begin{array}{ll}
z & \text { with prob } \kappa_{t} \\
x_{0} & \text { with prob }\left(1-\kappa_{t}\right)
\end{array} \quad\right. \text { mixture } \\
& p_{t}(d x | z)=\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}}\left[\delta_{\sigma_{t} x_{0}+\alpha_{t} z}\right] \quad \Leftrightarrow x_{t}=\sigma_{t} x_{0}+\alpha_{t} z \quad \text { geometric average }
\end{aligned}
$$

