Theorem 4.5. Let $\kappa  \in  \mathbb{R}$ . For an irreducible and reversible Markov kernel(X, K) the following assertions are equivalent:

1. $\operatorname{Ric}\left( K\right)  \geqq  \kappa$ ;

2. For all $\rho , v \in  \mathcal{P}\left( \mathcal{X}\right)$ , the following ‘evolution variational inequality’ holds for all $t \geqq  0$ :
$$ 
\frac{1}{2}\frac{{\mathrm{d}}^{ + }}{\mathrm{d}t}{\mathcal{W}}^{2}\left( {{P}_{t}\rho , v}\right)  + \frac{\kappa }{2}{\mathcal{W}}^{2}\left( {{P}_{t}\rho , v}\right)  \leqq  \mathcal{H}\left( v\right)  - \mathcal{H}\left( {{P}_{t}\rho }\right) ; 
$$ 

5. For all $\rho  \in  {\mathcal{P}}_{ * }\left( \mathcal{X}\right)$ we have
$$
\text{Hess}\mathcal{H}\left( \rho \right)  \geqq  \kappa \text{;}
